      Verification details:
      
      - Swift parsing now supports type and value parameter packs, including
      each/repeat expansions and pack constraints. Before: The pre-update
      Swift parser lacked pack productions and produced parsing errors for
      pack declarations, parameter types, constraints, and value expansions.
      Evidence: `OSS/tests/parsing/swift/parameter_packs.swift`,
      `OSS/tests/patterns/swift/pack_declaration.swift`,
      `OSS/tests/patterns/swift/parameter_packs.swift`
      - Swift parsing now supports if and switch expressions used as variable
      initializers. Before: The pre-update parser produced errors for these
      initializer expressions instead of representing their conditions and
      branches. Evidence:
      `OSS/tests/parsing/swift/conditional_expressions.swift`,
      `OSS/tests/patterns/swift/conditional_expressions.swift`,
      `OSS/tests/patterns/swift/switch_expression.swift`
      - Swift parsing now supports macro declarations with typed signatures
      and #externalMacro definitions. This does not implement macro expansion.
      Before: The pre-update grammar had no macro declaration production and
      produced parsing errors for the regression examples. Evidence:
      `OSS/tests/parsing/swift/macro_declarations.swift`,
      `OSS/tests/patterns/swift/macro_declarations.swift`
      - Swift property observers now retain their willSet/didSet bodies and
      parameters separately from property initializers. Before: The pre-update
      parser treated initialized property observers as trailing closures on a
      call to the initializer, and uninitialized observers as ordinary
      computed-property statements. Evidence:
      `OSS/tests/parsing/swift/property_observers.swift`,
      `OSS/tests/snapshots/semgrep-core/5d1a77f16853/stdout`,
      `OSS/tests/patterns/swift/property_observers.swift`
      - Swift parsing now supports borrowing, consuming, package, and
      distributed modifiers while preserving their distinct spellings. Before:
      These modifier alternatives were absent from the pre-update grammar; the
      ownership and visibility regression fixture produced parsing errors.
      Evidence: `OSS/tests/parsing/swift/ownership_modifiers.swift`,
      `OSS/tests/patterns/swift/ownership_modifiers.swift`,
      `OSS/tests/patterns/swift/package_modifier.swift`
      - Swift parsing now supports #unavailable conditions and distinguishes
      them from #available conditions. Before: The pre-update availability
      production accepted only #available and produced errors for
      #unavailable. Evidence:
      `OSS/tests/parsing/swift/unavailable_condition.swift`,
      `OSS/tests/patterns/swift/unavailable_condition.swift`
      - Swift parsing now supports member access on parenthesized existential
      types, such as (any P).self, and preserves the underlying parenthesized
      existential or opaque type. Before: The pre-update parser rejected (any
      P).self and represented parenthesized existential and opaque type
      annotations as single-field tuple types. Evidence:
      `OSS/tests/parsing/swift/parenthesized_types.swift`,
      `OSS/tests/snapshots/semgrep-core/d2114a6199c2/stdout`
      - Swift parsing now supports references to the bitwise AND operator
      using (&). Before: The pre-update parser interpreted (&) as a prefix
      expression with a missing operand rather than an operator reference.
      Evidence: `OSS/tests/parsing/swift/operator_contexts.swift`,
      `OSS/tests/patterns/swift/operator_reference.swift`
      
